{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new module extensions (Reactor processor support, message history interceptor, Protobuf codec) will adhere to existing Spring XD module development patterns to maintain consistency with the framework's architecture.",
    "The xd-yarn info command will reuse the pre-existing Zookeeper client utility already utilized by Spring XD YARN deployments to retrieve the admin port, eliminating the need for new Zookeeper integration work.",
    "The Reactor processor plugin will be built on Project Reactor 3.x (compatible with Spring Framework 6.0 and Java 17+) and follow the same module support structure as existing Spark and RxJava processor modules.",
    "The Protobuf codec will implement the standard Spring XD Codec interface to ensure seamless integration with existing module pipelines, and will accept user-provided protobuf message classes as a configurable module option.",
    "Message history tracking will leverage Spring Integration's HeaderEnricher pattern to add metadata to message headers, with a toggleable module option to enable or disable the feature per module configuration.",
    "The Ambari plugin will extend the existing Spring XD Ambari service definition and use the Ambari 2.7+ REST API and SDK to ensure compatibility with widely used Hadoop cluster management environments.",
    "JdbcHdfs job partition validation will be implemented as a JSR-303 bean validation method in the existing JdbcHdfsOptionsMetadata class, following the existing validation pattern used in the codebase.",
    "Performance testing for complex object serialization will use JMH (Java Microbenchmark Harness) to ensure accurate, reproducible performance measurements."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Existing Spring XD YARN deployments already store the admin server port in a predefined, accessible Zookeeper node, so no changes to YARN deployment logic are required for the info command to function.",
    "All required third-party dependencies (Project Reactor 3.x, protobuf-java, JMH, Ambari SDK) are compatible with Spring Framework 6.0 and Java 17+, and are available in the project's managed dependency repository.",
    "The existing xd-yarn script is a bash script with an established subcommand structure that can be extended to add the new 'info' subcommand without major refactoring.",
    "Users of the Reactor processor plugin will provide a valid Reactor Flux/Mono based processor implementation class and configure standard module options via the existing Spring XD module configuration mechanism.",
    "Users of the Protobuf codec will provide the correct protobuf message class corresponding to their data payloads and have protobuf schema definitions available for their use case.",
    "The test environment has access to a running YARN cluster, Zookeeper instance, Ambari server, and Hadoop cluster for integration testing of the new features.",
    "The Spring XD wiki is hosted on a platform that allows direct editing by the development team, so documentation updates can be completed without additional approval workflows.",
    "The existing JdbcHdfs job configuration validation is already integrated with the Spring XD job deployment pipeline, so adding the new @AssertTrue method will automatically enforce the validation rule without changes to the deployment flow."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement xd-yarn info command for YARN admin port",
      "activity_description": "Add a new 'info' subcommand to the existing xd-yarn bash script that queries Zookeeper using pre-existing Spring XD utilities to retrieve the admin server port for the current YARN deployment, outputs the port and admin URL to the console, and includes error handling for missing deployments or ZK connectivity issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Reactor processor plugin base support",
      "activity_description": "Create a ReactorProcessorModuleSupport base class following existing Spark/RxJava module patterns, abstract common Reactor setup (schedulers, error handling), add support for standard module options (concurrency, error channel), and include unit tests for the base class.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement message history tracking feature",
      "activity_description": "Add a configurable MessageHistoryInterceptor that enriches message headers with stream name, module name, and timestamp when enabled via module configuration, following Spring Integration header enricher patterns, with unit tests for enrichment logic and configuration toggling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Protocol Buffer codec option",
      "activity_description": "Create a ProtobufCodec class implementing the Spring XD Codec interface, support serialization/deserialization of user-provided protobuf message classes, add error handling for invalid protobuf data, and include unit tests for common protobuf use cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Add complex object test coverage and performance benchmarking",
      "activity_description": "Create test fixtures and test cases for complex object types (protobuf messages, nested POJOs, tree structures), use JMH to benchmark serialization/deserialization performance for each type, and document performance characteristics in test reports.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Ambari plugin for Spring XD cluster management",
      "activity_description": "Extend the existing Spring XD Ambari service definition to add provisioning, lifecycle management (start/stop/restart), and monitoring capabilities, implement Ambari REST API clients for cluster operations, add metrics collection for Spring XD modules, and include integration tests with a test Ambari server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Update JdbcHdfs partition validation logic",
      "activity_description": "Modify the JdbcHdfsOptionsMetadata class to add the specified @AssertTrue validation method to enforce mutual exclusivity of 'sql' and 'tableName' when 'partitionColumn' is set, update validation flow integration, and add unit tests for all validation scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Update wiki with partitioned job documentation",
      "activity_description": "Update the Spring XD wiki to document creation of partitioned JDBC-HDFS jobs, including usage of 'tableName'/'columns' and 'sql' options, explicit note of mutual exclusivity of 'sql' and 'tableName' for partitioned jobs, and code examples for each use case.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration testing and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end tests to verify all new features work together correctly, including testing the xd-yarn info command on YARN, Reactor processor in a stream, message history with protobuf codec, Ambari plugin operations, and partitioned job validation, fix any integration issues found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 25.0
  }
}

